  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3142328ce6992ba47b93a300cc2864ac, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC_Dialogue
  dialoguePanel: {fileID: 2520466111762878367}
  dialogueText: {fileID: 772327107}
  dialogue:
  - Instead of receiving gold medals or trophies, winners of the Ancient Olympic
    Games were crowned with a wreath woven from olive branches
  - Wreaths were not only worn by athletes, but also appeared in religious festivals,
    celebrations, and works of art as a symbol of great honour, wisdom, peace, achievement,
    and respect.
  - ' Olive trees were highly valued in Greece as they provided food, oil, wood,
    and shade.  '
  - 'Did you know? Olive trees were connected to the goddess Athena, who, according
    to Greek mythology, gifted the olive tree to the people of Athens! '
  contButton: {fileID: 1101970688}
  wordSpeed: 0.05
