MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1121106570}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3142328ce6992ba47b93a300cc2864ac, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC_Dialogue
  dialoguePanel: {fileID: 2520466111762878365}
  dialogueText: {fileID: 2071882835}
  dialogue:
  - Artists created mosaics by placing hundreds or even thousands of small pieces
    of stone, pottery, or glass together to make colorful and long lasting images.
  - Every small piece had to be placed by hand, requiring great patience and skill.
  - Although the Ancient Greeks created many paintings, very few have survived because
    they were often painted on wood or walls that disappeared over time.
  - Because they survived, they help historians understand what Greek paintings may
    have looked like.
  - "Did you know? A single mosaic could contain thousands of tiny pieces called
    \u2018tesserae.\u2019 "
  contButton: {fileID: 87512190}
  wordSpeed: 0.05
