    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'Greek builders created three famous column styles. They supported the
    roofs of temples and public buildings while also making them beautiful.

    The
    Doric column is the simplest style, with a plain top and a strong appearance.
    The Ionic column is easy to recognize because of the curled shapes, called volutes,
    at the top. The Corinthian column is the most decorative, with carved leaves
    that resemble the acanthus plant.

'
