  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 14
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 3
    m_MaxSize: 64
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: An amphora is a large clay jar that was used throughout Ancient Greece.
    Ancient Greeks used amphorae to carry olive oil, wine, water, and grain. Many
    were painted with exciting stories about heroes, gods, sports, and everyday life.
    Early Greek vases had simple patterns, but later artists painted detailed people
    and myths using black-figure and red-figure styles!
