    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: Artists created mosaics by placing hundreds or even thousands of small
    pieces of stone, pottery, or glass together to make colorful and long lasting
    images. Every small piece had to be placed by hand, requiring great patience
    and skill. Although the Ancient Greeks created many paintings, very few have
    survived because they were often painted on wood or walls that disappeared over
    time. Because they survived, they help historians understand what Greek paintings
    may have looked like.
