  m_Text: Greek statues changed a lot over time. Early statues from the Archaic Period
    stood stiff and straight. Many were created as grave markers or to honor the
    gods. During the Classical Period, artists became interested in making people
    look more natural. Later, during the Hellenistic Period, sculptures became even
    more expressive, with carved detailed facial expressions and dramatic poses!
    The Romans admired Greek sculptures so much that they created many copies, helping
    preserve artworks that would otherwise have been lost.
